diff --git a/docs/user/12-scan.md b/docs/user/12-scan.md
--- a/docs/user/12-scan.md
+++ b/docs/user/12-scan.md
@@ -34,7 +34,9 @@
 - Turn on [digital monitor](09-dmr.md) before you start the scan to stop on a call to any talkgroup, not only
   the channel's talkgroup and RX group list. It stays on at every channel and on the one the scan ends on. Pressing
   **Monitor** on a DMR channel during the scan turns it off or on for the rest of the scan.
-- On a signal the scan holds. It moves on 2 s after the signal ends, and stays if the signal comes back.
+- **Tools > Zone scan speed > Resume after call** sets how long a zone or VFO scan stays after a call ends.
+  Choose 0 to 10 s. The default is 2 s. The delay starts again each time a reply ends on the same channel.
+  Dual watch has its own delay.
 - Holding **Monitor** pauses the scan.

 ## While scanning
diff --git a/docs/spec/radio-features.md b/docs/spec/radio-features.md
--- a/docs/spec/radio-features.md
+++ b/docs/spec/radio-features.md
@@ -72,6 +72,8 @@
 Each stop: VFO, zone and dual-watch scans use a 25 ms settle to ignore readings from the previous frequency.
 Tools > Zone scan speed offers 25, 50, 75, 100, 150, 250 and 500 ms for empty channels. The default is 25 ms.
 The choice is saved and applies during a zone scan. VFO and dual watch use `scan_dwell_ms`.
+**Resume after call** in the same menu edits the existing `scan_delay_ms` setting for zone and VFO scans.
+The new delay applies to a running scan. Dual watch uses its independent delay.
 FM, P25, NXDN and YSF stops can use 25 ms. DMR needs at least 75 ms so the receiver gets three status readings
 across the TDMA slots. Dual watch holds each frequency for at least 150 ms.
 A signal is "active" when FM squelch opens (with the RX tone if the channel needs one) or DMR plays a call
